  "decisions": {
    "namespace": "Supersedes source article-purpose namespaces: article and collection default; user kind maps to user-article or user-collection per stored vector. Different IDs retain kind. Physical gate shared once per index.",
    "recipe": "Current live and foundation service write symmetric-r1 article only. Retained retrieval helper fails when not configured; incompatible same-physical recipe registry rejected. No task/model re-selection.",
    "repairs": "Per-entry provider overflow attribution keeps other short articles whole; body/text duplicate source keys deduplicate matching ETags; event-scoped B aggregate checkpoints prevent older scans completing newer work.",
    "interface": "VectorFoundationService articles/aggregate/preferences. No vectorEntityRefresh, refresh CLI, protected bulk API or new orchestration DDL imported.",
    "sourceBounds": "No total text/HTML ceiling. 32 KiB R2 transfer pages do not determine embeddings. Estimate whole candidates using multilingual-heuristic-r1, configured safety margin and JSON bytes; only proved oversized candidates bisect near sentence/paragraph boundaries. Persist remaining model candidates plus existing cursors/pools. Prewave 64 MiB reservations account for model candidate and raw page separately; HTML/PDF unchanged.",
    "rangeReplay": "Compare prepared range cursor to durable state under the existing writer lease before pooling; stale prepared pages retry without duplication. Large HTML uses bounded lexical URL pages rather than an unlimited seen set.",
    "wholeFirst": "Red regression produced 4/2/4 inputs for 70 KiB English / 48 KiB Chinese / 60 KiB mixed text; fixed output is one complete title/body input each. 8 KiB and 32 KiB transfers yield identical fragments. Real Workerd input-count and byte equality assertions pass, with 4 MiB-plus resume intact. Heuristic is not exact vendor tokenization; no new dependency or model download."
  },
